  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nA cold front approaching from SE Canada will push southeast \nacross the area during the afternoon to early evening hours. A \nfew light showers may occur in the W. Adirondacks, otherwise the\nfront will pass through dry with just increasing mid level \nclouds. Ahead of the front, temperatures expected to warm into \nthe mid to upper 60s in valley areas. Winds will shift to the \nnorthwest late in the day, with gusts of 15-20 mph developing, \nwith a few gusts to 25 mph. A colder air mass will filter in \ntonight into Wednesday with below normal temperatures. Another \nlarge area of high pressure will build SE from Canada, providing\ncontinued dry conditions. The high shifts south/east of our \nregion Wed night into Thu, with a milder S/SW flow developing. \nThis will allow temperatures to warm back to above normal \nlevels. Another moisture-starved cold front is expected to pass \nthrough Thu night into Fri, which may bring a few light showers \nto areas well north/west of Albany. Yet another area of high \npressure looks to build in over the upcoming weekend bringing \ntranquil weather, although temperatures are expected to remain \nslightly above normal.",
